course: dictionary
lesson: 4457
title: Happy and its many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word happy has more than one meaning. Its main meaning is feeling pleased, glad or full of joy. In «Happy Diwali» and «Eid Mubarak», it is used to wish someone well, not to describe a feeling.
explain: Read the words around happy to find its meaning. «The neighbour is happy to hand the ball back» uses happy to mean willing and pleased to do something. Ask yourself: is this sentence about a feeling, or is it wishing someone well?
explain: Happy can also describe how something makes you feel, as in «a happy ending». Once you know the common patterns, such as happy to, happy with and happy birthday, you will recognise them quickly.
fact: Happy means feeling pleased, glad or full of joy.
fact: «A happy ending» means an ending that makes you feel glad.
fact: «Happy to» means willing and pleased to do something, as in «I'm happy to help».
fact: Happy with means satisfied with something.
fact: Happiness is the noun, and happily is the adverb, as in «happily ever after».
exercise: In «Happy Diwali», what is happy doing? | *Wishing someone well at a festival | Feeling sad about the festival | Counting the lights | Running very fast
exercise: «The neighbour is happy to hand the ball back.» What does happy to mean here? | Satisfied with the price | Feeling joy in a sad story | *Willing and pleased to do something | Very loud
exercise: Find the noun that comes from happy. | happen | happily | happier | *happiness
test: «She was happy with her score.» What does happy with mean? | *Satisfied with it | Angry about it | Giving it away | Hiding it
test: Which word means the most happy? | happier | happily | *happiest | happiness
exam: The story ends «happily ever after». What does this tell you? | The story has no ending | *The characters are glad at the end | The story is about rain | The characters are sad at the end
